  "note": "Summer's authored material for the development engine (doc 24, The four seasons and The development engine; src/audio/music/develop/). The same shape as spring.json (read its note for what each field means), moved to F major, summer's home (Moon pull, summer's home tide, is in F), with summer's colors: the Lydian glow over IV (Bbmaj7#11), the warmer C9sus4, and the Mixolydian sway of Eb over the home bass (Eb/F). Approved with Matt, October 20, 2026. Additions over spring: tempo is per slot (summer's lift: mornings and interludes 70 to 84, evenings and nocturnes 58 to 72; default for any other), and palettes are per slot or weather, each a list of weighted choices (melody, accomp, bed, and optional counter), so in mornings and interludes the electric piano (fm-piano) takes the harmony a fifth of the time and the nylon guitar strums it about a third of the time (strum; strumBass false leaves out the piano's light bass, so the guitar plays alone over the bed). The guitar's other roles, a clean melody and a counter-harmony, come with the melody step (4b) and in the tides. figures.lines are short written chord lines the walk may play from home (develop.json harmony.lineChance, lineWeights): walk, the bass stepping down under F (F/Eb to F/D, the harmony carrying on from Dm); walk-down, the same walk on to C7sus4 (the bass F Eb D C); sway, Eb over the home bass and back to F; sus-turn (4/4) and sus-slow (3/4), Fsus4 to Fsus2 to F. Each bar of a line is a list of [symbol, place] chords, sharing the bar evenly; meters limits a line to those meters. Summer's own forms: sway (mornings and middays, long phrases that rock between F2 and Bb2) and long-dusk (evenings and nocturnes, six-bar phrases, two returns, a very low curve). The ending warm-hold lands on Fmaj7.",
